<title>GERMANY: Schering sees stronger betaferon sales.</title>
<headline>Schering sees stronger betaferon sales.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>German pharmaceuticals group Schering AG has raised its forecast for 1997 sales of Betaferon to over 600 million marks from 590 million, a spokeswoman said in response to Reuters enquiries.</p>
<p>The forecast for sales of 590 million marks was made in May. Analysts had expressed some scepticism as to the company's chances of meeting the goal given the launch of new competing products by other firms.</p>
<p>Betaferon is a multiple sclerosis drug.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
